00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:57.930
Yeah.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:03.330
So the whole approach
I'm building right now,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.530
it's a big--

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.020
I'm a consultant though.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.930
I'm not really directly
consulting as much right now,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.330
I'm supporting a lot
of our consultants.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.390
But as consultants,
they need to be

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:19.420
able to customize reports and
presentations for partners.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:23.940
So I built out a
system within Shiny

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.330
to actually populate
slide decks with metrics

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.710
and visualizations.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.530
And I can go on and
on about the reasons

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:35.070
why I took that approach,
but a big reason why

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:38.400
I wanted to have all of that
populate in Google Slide

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:43.080
decks was so that we can
customize the look and feel

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.790
and the story of any given
company's data specifically

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.780
tailored to them.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.650
And so yeah, I can go on and on
about why I chose that approach

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.780
over something like
parameterized reporting, which

00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:00.300
I'm also a big fan of, but yeah,
that's a big project of mine

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.020
right now.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.050
And then in addition to
that, we know each other

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.920
because I've been leading
a pretty major procurement

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.540
effort, and we're
in the final stages

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.860
now of installing
Posit software.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.840
So we're really
excited about that.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.380
But I learned a
lot about what it

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.100
takes to build a business
case for data science

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.520
tooling at your
organization, and getting buy

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.660
and across the org.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.900
And it's a pretty major
lift to get something

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.300
like that off the ground.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.220
What was one of
the biggest lessons

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.960
learned in building
business case?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.383
I would say--

00:05:39.383 --> 00:05:40.800
one of the biggest
lessons learned

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.720
in building the
business case was

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.760
have a flagship project that
ties to direct business value.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.910
So the project that
I'm doing really

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.060
helps automate a
lot of our processes

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.220
and makes it a lot faster
and easier and more

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.540
streamlined to populate these
decks with different data

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.710
insights.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.260
And so that was
enough of a driver

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.020
showcasing the
additional flexibility

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.350
that open source programming
tools offer us over a more

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.820
business intelligence tool.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:17.030
That was really a
big driver in what

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.710
led us to get this software.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.450
So I'd say having a project
that you can directly

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:28.790
tie to business value, that's
a big big learning from it.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:31.920
And then I'd say another
learning from it--

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.550
I would never have been able
to get this push through if I

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:37.760
didn't have a supportive
manager who really walked me

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.280
through the whole process
and helped me navigate

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:43.310
a lot of the
organizational hierarchy

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.330
to get something like
this off the ground.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.380
So finding and
developing your community

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.850
of allies that are also
interested in the same thing

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.020
as you.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.525
You're definitely not going
to be able to do this alone.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.790
