00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.450
the Python aspect of the app.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.850
And so, making
sure that we have,

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.860
whether it's a Conda
environment or some sort

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:56.320
of PIP environment, something
for the Python environment.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:59.110
So yeah, we're just ironing
out some of those deployment

00:12:59.110 --> 00:12:59.610
issues.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:03.210
But definitely a
very common problem.

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:06.930
I would say, I can't
quite speak to all

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.600
of the technical aspects
of that deployment,

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.120
but on the more
human side of things.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.030
One approach that
we've taken with how

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:18.750
we're deploying this app
out to our organization

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:22.500
is starting with our more
internal team and then kind

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.560
of slowly ramping it out
so that we don't just

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:29.790
open the floodgates to everyone
and then are kind of like,

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:30.940
putting out fires.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:35.610
But taking a more slow approach,
so that people know, "Hey we're

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:37.380
in the early stages
of deploying this,

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.080
we're still ironing
out the kinks."

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.890
I do know that our
DataOps engineers really

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.885
focused on making
sure that we employ

00:13:45.885 --> 00:13:49.062
a like, infrastructure-as-code
approach to how

00:13:49.062 --> 00:13:50.020
we're deploying things.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:53.190
So anywhere and everywhere that
we can kind of codify things

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.680
in Kubernetes, we are.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.440
So there's just a
lot of moving parts

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.560
to deploying an
app to production,

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:04.350
even if it's not partner-facing
production but just

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.280
internal use.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:10.020
And I think one of the
big, most important things

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.970
about deploying a
Shiny app like this

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.540
is want people to trust it.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:18.390
So I think taking the time and
really building in some buffer

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:20.400
so that you know
that the app is going

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.940
to be load-tested and
reliable all of these things,

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:28.530
before it goes out to
people, is a good practice

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:32.355
so that you don't deteriorate
trust in your data products.

00:14:32.355 --> 00:14:33.750
ISHWOR BHUSAL: Yeah, absolutely.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:34.250
I agree.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:37.200
And then, quite
frankly our team,

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.200
like from the
developer standpoint,

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:44.460
from data scientist and data
analysts standpoint, whenever

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.440
