00:48:05.390 --> 00:48:09.220
So the system I developed
for this reporting system is

00:48:09.220 --> 00:48:12.130
heavily, so it's like built
in the Rhino framework,

00:48:12.130 --> 00:48:15.700
but it borrows heavily
from Jiwan Heo,

00:48:15.700 --> 00:48:17.840
I think is how you
pronounce his last name.

00:48:17.840 --> 00:48:21.940
But he put out a blog
post on using R6 classes

00:48:21.940 --> 00:48:25.870
and Gargoyle triggers to
kind of manage reactivity

00:48:25.870 --> 00:48:27.850
within your app, and
I wanted to make sure

00:48:27.850 --> 00:48:31.330
that people weren't like
accidentally running

00:48:31.330 --> 00:48:32.840
a ton of database queries.

00:48:32.840 --> 00:48:38.200
So I built the system in a way
to when someone kind of selects

00:48:38.200 --> 00:48:40.090
their filters, they
select their filters,

00:48:40.090 --> 00:48:41.800
they click the action button.

00:48:41.800 --> 00:48:44.230
It runs a dbyplyer query.

00:48:44.230 --> 00:48:47.020
It saves the results
of that to an R6

00:48:47.020 --> 00:48:50.080
object that I then pass
around to different modules

00:48:50.080 --> 00:48:54.430
to build visualizations,
run analyzes, whatever,

00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:57.730
and then populate slide
decks by transferring it

00:48:57.730 --> 00:49:00.520
to the Google API.

00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:04.660
So there's a whole slew
of things there, yeah.

